  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UK Aid Match Fund III: Climate Resilient Agriculture (CAFOD costs)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is part of a consortium based programme in which 5 organisations are collaborating together to support poor women, men and children from hazard-prone or marginalised rural communities to adapt their livelihoods strategies to better cope with climate-related shocks and stresses. As the contract holder, CAFOD is responsible for coordinating the consortium, monitoring the programme and providing overall support to joint activities. CAFOD will recruit a Consortium Coordinator and Senior M&amp;E Officer in Bangladesh to support this programme. This project is for the operational costs incurred by CAFOD for activities such as the baseline, advocacy strategy development, consultant fees and annual workshops.</narrative>
  </description>
